## ⚡ STAGE 3: Async Kafka Event Mesh, KEDA Lag Autoscaler & AI Engine Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Trigger_Layer ["1. Explicit Human Trigger"]
        ClickBtn["🖱️ Quality Engineer Clicks 'Auto Balloon'\n(AI MUST NOT auto-start on upload)"]
        APIGateway[" Node.js API Gateway"]
    end

    subgraph Messaging_Layer ["2. Kafka Event Mesh & KEDA Scaler"]
        KafkaTopic[("📣 Apache Kafka Broker\nTopic: 'autoballoon.requested'")]
        KEDAOperator["☸️ KEDA ScaledObject Operator\n(Monitors Kafka Consumer Group Lag)"]
    end

    subgraph Compute_Layer ["3. Autoscale AI Extraction Worker Pool"]
        Worker1["🤖 AI Worker Container 1"]
        Worker2["🤖 AI Worker Container 2"]
        WorkerN["🤖 AI Worker Container N (0 -> 50 Pods)"]
    end

    subgraph Execution_Engine ["4. Deep Vision & Geometry Extraction"]
        ONNXOCR["🔍 ONNX Neural OCR Engine\n(Linear & Angular Dimensions)"]
        GDTAST["📐 ASME Y14.5 GD&T AST Parser\n(Datums A-Z, MMC/LMC Modifiers)"]
        RTreeOrbit["📍 Spatial R-Tree Orbiting Algorithm\n(Collision-Free Balloon Coordinates)"]
    end

    subgraph Sync_Layer ["5. Persistence & Live Sync"]
        PgBouncer["🔄 PgBouncer Pooler"]
        AuroraDB[("🐘 AWS Aurora PostgreSQL + PostGIS")]
        RedisPubSub[("⚡ Redis WebSockets PubSub")]
        NextJSUI[" Next.js WebSockets Client"]
    end

    ClickBtn --> APIGateway --> KafkaTopic
    KafkaTopic <--> KEDAOperator
    KEDAOperator -->|Scales 0-50 Pods| Worker1 & Worker2 & WorkerN
    Worker1 & Worker2 & WorkerN --> Execution_Engine
    Execution_Engine --> PgBouncer --> AuroraDB
    Execution_Engine --> RedisPubSub --> NextJSUI
```

### Stage 3 Execution Flow:
1. **Explicit "Auto Balloon" Click:** Processing starts **ONLY** when the engineer explicitly clicks the button.
2. **Kafka Event Publish:** API Gateway publishes an event to Kafka.
3. **KEDA Consumer Lag Autoscaling:** KEDA detects event lag and dynamically scales worker containers from **0 to 50 pods**.
4. **AI Vision Pipeline:** Workers run ONNX Neural OCR, parse ASME Y14.5 GD&T Feature Control Frames into ASTs, and compute spatial R-Tree balloon placement.
5. **Real-time Push:** Extracted characteristics are written to PostgreSQL via **PgBouncer** and pushed to the UI via **WebSockets (Redis PubSub)**.

